# 🌊 Lab 11 – One-Dimensional Convolutional Neural Network (1D CNN) for Time-Series Forecasting

> **Machine Learning Laboratory** | Forecasting electricity demand using a One-Dimensional Convolutional Neural Network (1D CNN).

---

## 📖 Overview

Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are not only effective for image processing but also powerful for analyzing sequential and time-series data. This laboratory introduces the implementation of a **One-Dimensional Convolutional Neural Network (1D CNN)** for forecasting electricity demand using the preprocessed **AEP Hourly Electricity Demand** dataset.

Unlike a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP), a 1D CNN can automatically extract meaningful local temporal patterns from sequential data through convolutional operations. This enables the model to capture short-term dependencies and improve forecasting performance.

The laboratory consists of a single Jupyter notebook demonstrating the complete workflow for building, training, and evaluating a 1D CNN forecasting model.

---

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes

After completing this laboratory, students will be able to:

- Understand the fundamentals of 1D Convolutional Neural Networks
- Prepare sequential input data for CNN models
- Design a Conv1D-based forecasting architecture
- Configure convolutional, pooling, dropout, and dense layers
- Train and validate deep learning models
- Apply callbacks for model checkpointing
- Generate predictions on unseen time-series data
- Evaluate forecasting performance using regression metrics
- Compare CNN-based forecasting with traditional neural networks

